<title>USA: Chic adopts shareholders rights plan.</title>
<headline>Chic adopts shareholders rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chic by H.I.S Inc said on Friday it adopted a shareholder rights plan to fend off any acquisition attempt that does not offer what it feels is fair value for the company's shares.</p>
<p>The plan becomes operable when somebody acquires 15 percent or more of the company's common stock without approval by Chic's independent directors, or when a tender offer is made that could result in 20 percent or more of the company's shares being acquired.</p>
<p>Chic makes and markets jeans.</p>
